From 2c66f1448f32f4c8bde21c326663d4ef554288cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:46:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] TFEL: device code support in the mathematical and material
 libraries

- TFEL_DEVICE_CODE macro, defined when device code is compiled, and
  host/device annotations of the mathematical objects, of the fixed size
  algorithms, of the eigen solvers of symmetric tensors (FSES included),
  of the non linear solvers and of the material tools (bounds checks,
  stress criteria, logarithmic strain handler, slip systems, finite
  strain tangent operators).
- tfel::fail and contract violations reported in device code, where
  exceptions are not supported; no recursion in the computation of the
  eigenvectors of symmetric tensors in device code.
- behaviours without virtual functions (MechanicalBehaviourConcept),
  slip systems built at compile time, trivially copyable classes
  (TrivialGenTypeBase, whose values are built in place,
  getConstantObject).
- numerical type of the generic interfaces: IsAssignableTo for narrower
  floating point types, size of the numerical type of a library read by
  ExternalLibraryManager.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
